{"id":"VHH__LightBox__compounds__LB_pointlight","collection":"VHH","category":"LightBox/compounds","source_path":"VHH/LightBox/compounds/LB_pointlight.json","root_names":["VHH::Tool::LB_pointlight"],"counts":{"nodes":63,"connections":134,"values":52,"overloads":1},"documentation_summary":"Component Compound - this compound is a light in the the LightBox system. Pointlight - This is a diffuse light generator that mimics the lighting from a point light. It does this by taking the direction from each point to the light and the mesh surface normal, performing a dot product and multiplying by the light's intensity. Then applying shadow information.","documentation_search":"LB pointlight Component Compound - this compound is a light in the the LightBox system. Pointlight - This is a diffuse light generator that mimics the lighting from a point light. It does this by taking the direction from each point to the light and the mesh surface normal, performing a dot product and multiplying by the light's intensity. Then applying shadow information. The diagnostic tab will hide and show the shadow rays to the light. Input input mesh The object you are lighting. accelerator You need to construct a raycast accelerator from the mesh to plug in here. pointLight position The position of the point light in world space. pointLight intensity Intensity and color of the point light. pointLight falloff distance The distance to which the light's intensity will falloff to zero. This is in worldspace units and is an inverse square falloff. pointLight weight This is an overall multiplier of the output. It is a auto-port, allowing for the input of float , floatArray and scalar field data. black array This port is intended for use in the LightBox system. It is an array of value {0,0,0} that the light result will be added to, can be left unconnected. Output point contribution An array of values, per point, of this light's contribution to the lighting. Add this to the point color of your mesh to see the result. light data The light data output as an object. This is intended for use with LB display .","port_names":["accelerator","black_array","input_mesh","light_data","pointLight_falloff_distance","pointLight_intensity","pointLight_position","pointLight_weight","point_contribution"],"node_types_search":["Core::Array::array_is_empty","Core::Array::array_size","Core::Array::filter_array","Core::Array::find_all_true_in_array","Core::Array::resize_array","Core::Array::set_in_array","Core::Constants::one","Core::Graph::pass","Core::Graph::terminal","Core::Logic::if","Core::Logic::not","Core::Math::add","Core::Math::divide","Core::Math::dot","Core::Math::length_squared","Core::Math::max","Core::Math::multiply","Core::Math::normalize","Core::Math::subtract","Core::Object::set_property","Core::Type_Conversion::to_float","Diagnostic::Display::location_scope","Geometry::Common::interpret_auto_port_as_scalar","Geometry::Mesh::get_mesh_structure","Geometry::Mesh::update_face_normals","Geometry::Mesh::update_mesh_normals","Geometry::Properties::get_point_count","Geometry::Properties::get_point_position","Geometry::Query::sample_property","Geometry::Query::sample_raycast_accelerator","Modeling::Primitive::create_mesh_sphere","Modeling::Strands::create_arrow_strands","Unknown","apply_light","bake_point_light","calculate_falloff","display","input_weight_data_handling","light_equation","mesh_info","pre_calc_ray","shadow_calc_PL1","to_light_info"],"dependencies_search":[],"roots":[{"overload_index":0,"name":"VHH::Tool::LB_pointlight","uri_imported":"file:///LB_pointlight.json","is_default_overload":null,"metadata":{"documentation":"../docs/LB_pointlight.md"},"documentation_file":"VHH/LightBox/docs/LB_pointlight.md","documentation":"### ***LB_pointlight***\n**Component Compound** - this compound is a light in the the LightBox system.<br /><br />\n**Pointlight** - This is a diffuse light generator that mimics the lighting from a *point* light.  It does this by taking the direction from each point to the light and the mesh surface normal, performing a dot product and multiplying by the light's intensity.  Then applying shadow information.<br /><br />\nThe diagnostic tab will hide and show the shadow rays to the light.<br />\n\n***\n## Input\n<span style=\"color:#90A3F4\">***input_mesh***</span>\n<br />The object you are lighting.\n\n<span style=\"color:#90A3F4\">***accelerator***</span>\n<br />You need to construct a raycast accelerator from the mesh to plug in here.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***pointLight_position***</span>\n<br />The position of the point light in world space.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***pointLight_intensity***</span>\n<br />Intensity and color of the point light.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***pointLight_falloff_distance***</span>\n<br />The distance to which the light's intensity will falloff to zero.  This is in worldspace units and is an inverse square falloff.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***pointLight_weight***</span>\n<br />This is an overall multiplier of the output.  It is a auto-port, allowing for the input of `float`, `floatArray` and `scalar_field` data.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***black_array***</span>\n<br />This port is intended for use in the LightBox system.  It is an array of value {0,0,0} that the light result will be added to, can be left unconnected.\n\n***\n## Output\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***point_contribution***</span>\n<br />An array of values, per point, of this light's contribution to the lighting.  Add this to the `point_color` of your mesh to see the result.\n\n<span style=\"color:#90A3F4\">***light_data***</span>\n<br />The light data output as an object.  This is intended for use with `LB_display`.","ports":[{"name":"input_mesh","direction":"input","type":"Object"},{"name":"accelerator","direction":"input","type":"Object"},{"name":"pointLight_position","direction":"input","type":"Math::float3","default":{"x":"0f","y":"0f","z":"0f"}},{"name":"pointLight